        },
        {
          "id": "isr-blocking#real-storage",
          "entrypoints": ["handler.ts", "node-server.ts"],
          "class": "L2",
          "port": 8241,
          "runner": "isr-real-storage",
          "storage": { "kind": "isr" },
          "serve": {
            "kind": "node",
            "cwd": "ts",
            "args": ["examples/isr-blocking/node-server.ts"]
          },
          "gap": "S3 and DynamoDB are emulated by the digest-pinned s3proxy and DynamoDB Local. DynamoDB Local does not perform TTL deletion, so the stored ttl attribute never expires an item; s3proxy has no bucket policies, IAM or event notifications. No real AWS endpoint is reached. The TableTheory adapter's invalidate() stays unsupported.",
          "description": "Blocking ISR on real local storage: S3HtmlStore on s3proxy plus the TableTheory metadata/lease store on DynamoDB Local, with the stored object and item asserted and the lease-held refusal exercised."
        }
      ]
    },
